  "notes": "Composed of {打|だ} (strike, hit) + {鍵|けん} (key). Used for both keyboard typing and piano playing. Common collocations: {打鍵|だけん}する (to type/strike keys), {打鍵|だけん}{速度|そくど} (typing speed), {打鍵|だけん}{数|すう} (number of keystrokes), {打鍵|だけん}{音|おん} (keystroke sound). In the mechanical keyboard community, {打鍵|だけん}{感|かん} (key feel) and {打鍵|だけん}{音|おん} (key sound) are important qualities. For piano, {打鍵|だけん} refers to the technique of striking the keys, distinct from the more general {演奏|えんそう} (performance).",
